adjudication.rationale:
In store.js.es6, the new plural hydration branch matches keys like *_ids and does:

```js
const hydrated = obj[k].map(id => self._lookupSubType(subType, type, id, root));
obj[self.pluralize(subType)] = hydrated || [];
delete obj[k];
```

Unlike the singular *_id case (which only assigns/deletes when a hydrated object is found), the plural case unconditionally deletes the original *_ids and will populate the new pluralized property with an array that can contain null/undefined entries whenever `_lookupSubType` can't find an id in the side-loaded `root` payload. That is a behavior change introduced by the diff and can leave consumers with a list containing nulls and no remaining id list to retry/recover from.
